Package: mica-storage-ubi
Version: 13.8+deb13u7-mica4
Source-Date-Epoch: 1794341201
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Provides: e2fsprogs, fdisk
Conflicts: e2fsprogs, fdisk
Description: Mica OS storage in UBI on raw NAND: no ext4 or partition tools, log in RAM
 A board that keeps its system in UBI volumes on raw NAND has DATA on UBIFS and
 no partition table: there is no ext4 file system for e2fsck or resize2fs and no
 partition for sfdisk to grow. This package provides
 e2fsprogs, which mica-system depends on for an ext4 DATA, and fdisk, which
 mica-openrc depends on to grow DATA's partition, so a root for such a board
 installs neither.
 .
 Nothing on that board runs them: mica-openrc grows DATA only where the board
 names its partitions, checks only the file systems /etc/fstab gives a pass
 number and grows only those marked x-systemd.growfs, and a UBI board does none
 of that. A product that wants e2fsprogs or fdisk itself installs them in place
 of this package.
 .
 Its one file, /usr/lib/mica/log/log.d/10-ubi.env, keeps the system log in RAM by
 default (LOG_PERSISTENT=no): raw NAND wears with every write, and its DATA is
 small. micad's log settings may still turn it on.
